// `c.rue` and `w.rue` each export two different modules `m`, so `m` is ambiguous in each. `d.rue`
// exports `X` through `c.rue`'s `m` by name, and `e.rue` everything in `w.rue`'s with a glob
// export. In `c.rue` the glob export that binds `m` comes first, and in `w.rue` it comes second.
// Either way, the files' exports could refer to the `X` in either module, so none of the `X`s is
// reported as unused. Only `z.rue`'s `m` has a `W`, which `e.rue` exports only when `w.rue`'s
// `m` is bound to it, but it could be either way, so it isn't reported either. `a.rue`'s `W` is
// only in a module that `d.rue` doesn't export everything from, so it's reported.

fn main() -> Int {
    3
}
